{
  "source": "edited",
  "logic": "Each case states database rows as in sync/admin-manifest.json (input: now, donors, payments, donations and, where the computation reads them, links and symbolClaims) and, in input.chunks, the rows of every chunk of the administration's device copy the computation reads, keyed <part>/<chunk id> as the device stores them (donations/payments:<yyyy-mm>, donations/donations:<yyyy-mm>, donations/donor-records:<yyyy-mm>, donations/links:<yyyy-mm>, donations/symbol-claims, donations/receipts:<year>, donors/accounts:<yyyy-mm>), with ids aliased as CaseRows names them. The backend runner writes the rows, checks that the sync endpoints answer exactly input.chunks (and input.summary where given), then asks the endpoint for every query of input.queries; the browser runner computes each answer from input.chunks alone. Both compare the whole list of answers with expected.answers. The computation is the donor search of pairing a payment, GET /api/admin/donations/donors?query=: a query blank after trimming finds nobody; otherwise every donor record that is not erased whose name, with the Czech accented letters folded to plain ones and lowercased, contains the query folded the same way, or whose variable symbol starts with the trimmed query, both matched literally (a percent sign or an underscore is no wildcard), ordered by name and then donor id, at most 20, each as donorId, name, type, variableSymbol and companyIdentifier. The server orders names by the database collation and the browser by the Czech one; the cases keep to names both order alike.",
